1
00:00:01,042 --> 00:00:06,381
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,052 --> 00:00:14,931
[Jaguar] <i>It's just the start.</i>
<i>We'll take all of the Ardientes' money.</i>

3
00:00:15,015 --> 00:00:16,975
<i>We'll milk them dry.</i>

4
00:00:17,058 --> 00:00:19,602
-[man 1] <i>For the Jaguar!</i>
-[other men] <i>Jaguar!</i>

5
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:23,314
[Julio] <i>An armed group of men</i>
<i>broke into our gambling den.</i>

6
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:27,569
<i>And the leader of this group</i>
<i>calls himself Jaguar.</i>

7
00:00:27,652 --> 00:00:30,280
<i>Miss Camia, you don't know how happy</i>
<i>you're going to make me</i>

8
00:00:30,363 --> 00:00:32,240
<i>if you let me work for you!</i>

9
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:34,325
<i>-All right.</i>
<i>-Thank you, Miss Camia!</i>

10
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:36,703
[Arnaldo] <i>A lifetime</i>
<i>of love and happiness.</i>

11
00:00:36,786 --> 00:00:38,788
<i>Ivy Aguas, will you marry me?</i>

12
00:00:38,872 --> 00:00:40,790
[Ivy] <i>Yes, Arnaldo. I will marry you.</i>

13
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:43,918
<i>How will I bring the Ardientes down?</i>

14
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:46,171
<i>Step one: make their favorite</i>
<i>grandson fall for me,</i>

15
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:49,090
<i>and use him against them.</i>

16
00:00:49,174 --> 00:00:51,468
<i>Achievement unlocked.</i>

17
00:00:51,551 --> 00:00:53,303
[man] <i>Jaguar. The boss is here…</i>

18
00:00:53,386 --> 00:00:55,388
[Natalie] <i>Mr. Jaguar?</i>

19
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:57,182
<i>What a cool name.</i>

20
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:01,102
[Nimfa] <i>I think I've earned her trust.</i>

21
00:01:01,186 --> 00:01:02,854
<i>Don't worry, Governor.</i>

22
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:05,690
<i>We'll learn all of Camia Cruz's secrets.</i>

23
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:07,942
<i>Even who her backer is.</i>

24
00:01:08,026 --> 00:01:10,487
[Emilia] <i>I already know it's Ivy Aguas.</i>

25
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:11,780
[Diego] <i>Is it true?</i>

26
00:01:11,863 --> 00:01:13,782
<i>Are you going to marry Arnaldo?</i>

27
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:14,908
<i>Yes.</i>

28
00:01:14,991 --> 00:01:16,409
[Diego] <i>You're going to marry the man</i>

29
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:17,952
<i>who might've killed Nanny Carlotta?</i>

30
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:19,788
<i>I'm sorry, Ivy. But I'd do anything</i>

31
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:21,790
<i>to stop you from marrying Arnaldo!</i>

32
00:01:21,873 --> 00:01:23,083
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

33
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:24,793
<i>I just love you too much.</i>

34
00:01:29,464 --> 00:01:32,801
[ominous music playing]

35
00:01:35,178 --> 00:01:36,513
[line rings]

36
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:38,389
Is she all right?

37
00:01:38,473 --> 00:01:40,099
Why isn't she picking up?

38
00:01:45,188 --> 00:01:47,982
Miss Camia, I brought you tea.

39
00:01:49,567 --> 00:01:52,570
I wanted to apologize
for what happened earlier.

40
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:55,073
Don't worry about it, Nimfa.

41
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:57,242
Just don't do it again, okay?

42
00:01:58,034 --> 00:01:58,868
Yes.

43
00:01:59,744 --> 00:02:00,912
[sighs]

44
00:02:04,874 --> 00:02:06,376
You can't make a call?

45
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:09,963
I noticed that there's no reception here.

46
00:02:10,046 --> 00:02:11,714
I can go with you outside

47
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:14,968
so you can call whoever it is
you're trying to reach.

48
00:02:15,051 --> 00:02:16,177
No, it's fine.

49
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:18,721
I'm going to take a shower,
then I'm off to bed.

50
00:02:18,805 --> 00:02:20,223
You should head home.

51
00:02:20,306 --> 00:02:22,016
Have the driver drop you off.

52
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:23,518
-Okay.
-You can leave that there.

53
00:02:23,601 --> 00:02:24,519
Okay.

54
00:02:24,602 --> 00:02:27,689
[ominous music playing]

55
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:37,448
Oh! It spilled!

56
00:02:37,532 --> 00:02:39,909
-I'm sorry! I spilled the tea!
-What happened?

57
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:41,536
I spilled the tea.

58
00:02:41,619 --> 00:02:43,705
Don't worry, ma'am.
I'll take care of this.

59
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:45,707
I'll get this fixed
by the time you're done.

60
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:47,625
I'm so sorry.

61
00:02:47,709 --> 00:02:49,043
-Okay.
-Oh, my.

62
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:52,922
[ominous music playing]

63
00:03:05,476 --> 00:03:08,438
[suspenseful music playing]

64
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:39,802
[tense music playing]

65
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:51,522
[suspenseful music playing]

66
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:06,287
[phone ringing]

67
00:04:06,371 --> 00:04:07,956
[line rings]

68
00:04:08,039 --> 00:04:12,168
[ringing continues]

69
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:15,171
[suspenseful music continues]

70
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:28,643
Nimfa!

71
00:04:30,061 --> 00:04:31,062
Who's on the phone?

72
00:04:36,442 --> 00:04:38,778
Oh! Miss Camia.

73
00:04:40,446 --> 00:04:42,573
What are you doing with my phone?

74
00:04:43,116 --> 00:04:45,034
And why did you answer that call?

75
00:04:45,535 --> 00:04:48,788
Uh… I thought it was someone important.

76
00:04:50,248 --> 00:04:52,041
Someone named "A" was calling.

77
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:54,043
Who is that?

78
00:04:55,169 --> 00:04:57,046
Nimfa, just go home.

79
00:04:57,547 --> 00:05:01,009
And don't touch my phone next time, okay?

80
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:04,095
Go on.

81
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:06,806
[tense music playing]

82
00:05:10,351 --> 00:05:11,602
[door closes]

83
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:17,900
-Hello, dear.
-Mom?

84
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:19,777
I'm sorry, dear.

85
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:21,696
Nimfa got a hold of my phone.

86
00:05:21,779 --> 00:05:24,949
I heard! Why was she
going through your stuff?

87
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:27,076
<i>Mom, I know we've known her for a while,</i>

88
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:29,704
but we can't just trust her.

89
00:05:30,288 --> 00:05:31,414
It's risky.

90
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,249
<i>We can't just trust…</i>

91
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:36,377
the people around us.

92
00:05:36,461 --> 00:05:38,087
Is that why you've become particular

93
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:40,006
with our bodyguards too?

94
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:42,091
Yes, Mom!

95
00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:43,926
Because our former bodyguards

96
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:46,262
couldn't even protect Nanny Carlotta!

97
00:05:46,345 --> 00:05:49,182
<i>If something bad happens…</i>

98
00:05:49,265 --> 00:05:50,975
I know I can protect myself.

99
00:05:51,392 --> 00:05:52,977
But you, Mom…

100
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:55,938
I want you to be extra careful. Please.

101
00:05:56,647 --> 00:05:58,357
Even from people like Nimfa.

102
00:05:58,983 --> 00:05:59,984
<i>Please.</i>

103
00:06:00,359 --> 00:06:02,695
Okay, dear. I'll be careful.

104
00:06:02,779 --> 00:06:04,572
And I'll try to get to know her more.

105
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:06,616
Yes, Mom. Please.

106
00:06:07,158 --> 00:06:08,409
Okay, bye.

107
00:06:08,743 --> 00:06:11,496
[unsettling music playing]

108
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:22,590
[ominous music playing]

109
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:30,389
-Give it to them.
-Yes, Boss.

110
00:06:35,269 --> 00:06:36,854
You're the best, Mr. Jaguar!

111
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:38,731
Thanks for this!

112
00:06:39,107 --> 00:06:40,775
-Thanks, sir!
-Thanks, sir!

113
00:06:40,858 --> 00:06:41,692
Thanks, sir!

114
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:44,946
There's more where that came from.

115
00:06:45,029 --> 00:06:49,659
If you do your jobs properly
and remain loyal to me,

116
00:06:50,243 --> 00:06:53,579
I guarantee, you'll all be
swimming in a pool of money.

117
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:56,374
You can count on us, Mr. Jaguar.

118
00:06:56,457 --> 00:06:58,084
Right, boys?

119
00:06:58,167 --> 00:06:59,252
Cheers, boys!

120
00:06:59,335 --> 00:07:00,962
Cheers!

121
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:03,756
[tense music playing]

122
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:08,594
[Arnaldo] I want everyone
to be present at dinner.

123
00:07:08,678 --> 00:07:10,221
This is very important to me.

124
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:12,807
I think I know what this is about.

125
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:14,016
But don't worry.

126
00:07:14,892 --> 00:07:16,185
I won't preempt you.

127
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:19,564
[Julio] Oh, and by the way…

128
00:07:20,231 --> 00:07:23,985
Don't expect your father
to be there tomorrow.

129
00:07:24,402 --> 00:07:26,487
Well, I don't really care
about him, so it's fine.

130
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:29,365
No, since you're requiring
everyone to be present,

131
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:30,700
I'll make sure your father's there.

132
00:07:30,783 --> 00:07:32,910
I'll invite him. He'll be there.

133
00:07:32,994 --> 00:07:34,162
[chuckles]

134
00:07:34,745 --> 00:07:40,501
I wonder whose bed Raul
is sleeping on right now.

135
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:43,087
Emilia,

136
00:07:43,171 --> 00:07:47,216
I bet your husband's sleeping
with yet another woman.

137
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:51,429
Papa, believe it or not, Raul has changed.

138
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:53,806
-What?
-Yes, Papa!

139
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:59,353
In fact, he actually wants us
to renew our vows.

140
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:01,481
[laughs sarcastically]

141
00:08:02,106 --> 00:08:04,859
[Julio and Arnaldo laughing]

142
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:08,070
That's the dumbest idea I've heard

143
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:09,989
since "women empowerment."

144
00:08:10,781 --> 00:08:13,326
Do you seriously still believe Raul?

145
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,995
He's been feeding you nothing but lies,

146
00:08:16,078 --> 00:08:18,164
and yet here you are,

147
00:08:18,247 --> 00:08:20,708
crazy enough to believe
his empty promises!

148
00:08:23,252 --> 00:08:25,129
I just don't get it!

149
00:08:29,133 --> 00:08:32,428
[ominous music playing]

150
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:47,652
I'm sure Emilia's going to like this.

151
00:08:48,694 --> 00:08:51,822
I just know she won't suspect anything…

152
00:08:52,448 --> 00:08:54,992
when I give this to her.

153
00:08:56,244 --> 00:08:59,664
Well, I have a better idea.

154
00:09:01,249 --> 00:09:02,708
What if…

155
00:09:05,044 --> 00:09:09,465
you choke your wife with this necklace?

156
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:15,513
Choke her until her eyes pop out.

157
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:17,848
[grunts]

158
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:20,393
[laughs]

159
00:09:20,476 --> 00:09:21,978
What do you think?

160
00:09:25,356 --> 00:09:27,275
Well, Raul…

161
00:09:27,358 --> 00:09:28,985
I can't keep waiting.

162
00:09:30,736 --> 00:09:35,074
I want to rip Emilia's face apart

163
00:09:35,157 --> 00:09:36,951
and bury her alive.

164
00:09:37,034 --> 00:09:39,787
[ominous music playing]

165
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:43,374
Just wait a little more, Natalie.

166
00:09:44,542 --> 00:09:48,379
Once we get all the Ardientes' wealth,

167
00:09:48,462 --> 00:09:52,717
including their illegal properties,

168
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:55,303
we will take control of everything.

169
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:58,431
I will be the king…

170
00:10:00,224 --> 00:10:02,268
and you will be my queen.

171
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:05,730
I trust you.

172
00:10:08,232 --> 00:10:10,985
But my impatience
may get the better of me.

173
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,279
So, be fast.

174
00:10:15,656 --> 00:10:17,575
You shouldn't keep me waiting.

175
00:10:17,658 --> 00:10:20,453
[tense music playing]

176
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:33,466
[groans]

177
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,469
-Emilia, hello.
-Where have you been?

178
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:38,596
Didn't I mention--

179
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:40,389
I just noticed, Raul,

180
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:42,725
you always keep me waiting here.

181
00:10:42,808 --> 00:10:44,268
-Where have you been?
-I told you…

182
00:10:44,352 --> 00:10:46,187
I'd just check on my business.

183
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:47,229
Liar!

184
00:10:47,313 --> 00:10:49,523
No, Emilia. What?

185
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:53,694
Do I smell like a baby?

186
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,321
Well?

187
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:57,365
Give me your phone.

188
00:10:58,574 --> 00:11:00,493
-I don't understand--
-Give it to me!

189
00:11:01,869 --> 00:11:03,579
What's wrong with you, Emilia?

190
00:11:10,044 --> 00:11:12,671
What now? Go on, check all of it.

191
00:11:13,672 --> 00:11:15,508
Did you find something?

192
00:11:16,717 --> 00:11:18,677
Are you done now?

193
00:11:20,471 --> 00:11:21,722
Now, it's my turn.

194
00:11:23,891 --> 00:11:25,142
Let me do this.

195
00:11:26,811 --> 00:11:28,104
You know, Emilia…

196
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:31,023
when I told you I would change,

197
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:33,234
I meant it.

198
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:37,154
Well, I don't believe
any single word that you say.

199
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:39,156
I know you're just fooling me.

200
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:42,493
Wait.

201
00:11:42,576 --> 00:11:45,329
[unsettling music playing]

202
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:47,790
[exhales]

203
00:11:48,457 --> 00:11:50,292
I have something for you.

204
00:11:51,377 --> 00:11:53,712
Maybe by giving this to you,

205
00:11:53,796 --> 00:11:55,423
you won't get mad at me anymore.

206
00:11:56,048 --> 00:11:57,049
Hmm?

207
00:11:58,759 --> 00:12:01,053
That's the business I was talking about.

208
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:04,557
We have diamonds and jewelry.

209
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:08,227
Come on, smile!

210
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:11,939
You even tried to smell me, huh?

211
00:12:12,022 --> 00:12:14,650
[chuckles]

212
00:12:15,234 --> 00:12:16,694
Where's my phone?

213
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:20,281
-Wait. See? I knew it!
-[phone rings]

214
00:12:20,364 --> 00:12:22,074
Is this your new mistress?!

215
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:23,701
-I told you, I'm right.
-Emilia…

216
00:12:27,121 --> 00:12:29,039
Raul, I have a suggestion for you.

217
00:12:29,665 --> 00:12:31,083
Since you want to have a new business,

218
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:32,835
why don't you put up a funeral home?

219
00:12:32,918 --> 00:12:34,795
You know why? You'll earn a lot more.

220
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:37,298
Because I'll have
all your mistresses killed!

221
00:12:37,381 --> 00:12:38,924
Give me that, I need to answer--

222
00:12:39,008 --> 00:12:40,009
Wait!

223
00:12:40,676 --> 00:12:41,677
Hello?

224
00:12:43,137 --> 00:12:44,096
<i>Yes.</i>

225
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:47,266
<i>This is Governor Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

226
00:12:47,349 --> 00:12:48,976
The wife of Raul.

227
00:12:49,059 --> 00:12:50,644
<i>This is to inform you</i>

228
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:52,146
that I've already scheduled your funeral.

229
00:12:52,229 --> 00:12:53,689
See you!

230
00:12:53,772 --> 00:12:56,400
[unsettling music playing]

231
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:00,237
Give me that!

232
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:04,283
Do you know who that was?

233
00:13:05,159 --> 00:13:06,994
That was my boss.

234
00:13:07,077 --> 00:13:09,079
He's the one doing business with me.

235
00:13:09,163 --> 00:13:10,623
With all the diamonds and jewelry.

236
00:13:12,082 --> 00:13:16,295
How can I succeed if you don't
trust me in the first place?

237
00:13:16,378 --> 00:13:18,589
Didn't I tell you
I'd change for the better?

238
00:13:20,174 --> 00:13:21,467
Emilia…

239
00:13:22,676 --> 00:13:24,720
How many times do I need
to tell you I love you?

240
00:13:27,264 --> 00:13:28,224
[sighs]

241
00:13:28,307 --> 00:13:31,310
[tense music playing]

242
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,149
[sighs]

243
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:43,656
[deep sigh]

244
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:46,617
[tense music playing]

245
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,418
[Arnaldo] Go on, just put it there.

246
00:13:56,502 --> 00:13:57,962
-What's that?
-Before she comes down.

247
00:13:58,045 --> 00:14:00,381
-Get the rest inside too.
-Arnaldo?

248
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:03,342
What's this? What's happening?

249
00:14:03,425 --> 00:14:04,510
Good morning!

250
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:08,472
Good morning, but what's happening?

251
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:11,559
Well, I hired some new maids for you.

252
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:14,436
Just to help you maintain this house

253
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:15,813
since Carlotta's gone.

254
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:18,524
[tense music playing]

255
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:24,864
[groans]

256
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:28,367
Hon, thank you.

257
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:29,827
I appreciate it.

258
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:32,788
But I don't need new maids.

259
00:14:32,872 --> 00:14:35,040
I can manage here alone.

260
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:38,085
No, you don't have to do that.

261
00:14:40,921 --> 00:14:42,298
Why not?

262
00:14:42,381 --> 00:14:43,591
Wait.

263
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:49,763
Do you think that ruthless
murderer will come back here?

264
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:52,975
Well, hon, let me tell you this.

265
00:14:53,058 --> 00:14:54,435
I'm not afraid to face them.

266
00:14:54,518 --> 00:14:57,479
Because with all the knives I have here,

267
00:14:57,563 --> 00:14:59,064
I can return the favor.

268
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:01,025
I'm not afraid of them!

269
00:15:01,108 --> 00:15:03,777
[tense music playing]

270
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:07,448
Hey, hon.

271
00:15:08,365 --> 00:15:09,867
Are you okay?

272
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:11,368
Yeah, I'm okay.

273
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:12,912
Uh…

274
00:15:13,370 --> 00:15:15,581
I was just thinking…

275
00:15:15,664 --> 00:15:17,291
maybe…

276
00:15:17,374 --> 00:15:18,959
you don't need to be alone.

277
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:22,254
So, after our wedding,

278
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:24,965
I'd like you to move in
with me into the mansion.

279
00:15:27,259 --> 00:15:29,720
I'd love that! But, the question is…

280
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:32,097
Will Emilia be okay
with me being the new queen

281
00:15:32,181 --> 00:15:33,891
of the Ardientes' mansion?

282
00:15:33,974 --> 00:15:36,352
Well, like I said,
no one cares what she thinks.

283
00:15:36,894 --> 00:15:38,854
And she's no longer queen.

284
00:15:39,855 --> 00:15:41,023
You are.

285
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,525
Aw, hon!

286
00:15:43,984 --> 00:15:45,152
Thank you.

287
00:15:46,111 --> 00:15:48,364
You are such a sweet fiancé.

288
00:15:48,864 --> 00:15:50,032
Come here.

289
00:15:53,035 --> 00:15:54,620
Okay. Let's eat.

290
00:15:55,245 --> 00:15:56,956
Oops! You sit here.

291
00:15:57,039 --> 00:16:00,668
You aren't my husband yet,
but soon, you will be.

292
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:01,919
[laughs]

293
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:03,045
Okay.

294
00:16:04,797 --> 00:16:06,465
Aww, thank you, hon.

295
00:16:09,677 --> 00:16:12,012
Do you want juice or coffee?

296
00:16:14,056 --> 00:16:15,182
Yeah.

297
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:19,561
Well, hon, you have to bring
your maids with you.

298
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:23,065
You need to follow the queen's orders.

299
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,442
Or else, there won't be a wedding.

300
00:16:25,526 --> 00:16:26,652
[sighs]

301
00:16:29,655 --> 00:16:31,198
I love you.

302
00:16:31,281 --> 00:16:32,908
Well, I love you more.

303
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:34,243
[chuckles]

304
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:40,416
Aunt Camia, let's push through
with the case.

305
00:16:40,749 --> 00:16:43,794
Arthur and I can testify
against the Ardientes.

306
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:45,838
I'll spill all their dirt!

307
00:16:47,464 --> 00:16:49,091
Diego, hold on.

308
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:50,467
Let's not be too impulsive.

309
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:54,013
What's going on?
Why are you acting like this?

310
00:16:56,598 --> 00:16:58,058
It's about Ivy.

311
00:16:58,392 --> 00:17:01,020
[unsettling music playing]

312
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:04,314
She's getting married to Arnaldo.

313
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,486
We can't let that happen.

314
00:17:10,404 --> 00:17:12,322
Aunt Camia, we have to stop Ivy.

315
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:15,659
[tense music playing]

316
00:17:23,459 --> 00:17:24,626
It's pretty…

317
00:17:25,669 --> 00:17:27,463
and full of crap.

318
00:17:27,838 --> 00:17:30,632
Aunt Claire, stop being so negative.

319
00:17:31,175 --> 00:17:34,178
-Wasn't this sweet of Raul?
-[scoffs]

320
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:36,430
Manipulating.

321
00:17:37,806 --> 00:17:39,600
Focus on your goal, Emilia!

322
00:17:40,142 --> 00:17:41,727
Bring Camia Cruz down,

323
00:17:41,810 --> 00:17:44,021
so you can earn Julio's approval.

324
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:47,149
I haven't forgotten
about that, Aunt Claire.

325
00:17:47,232 --> 00:17:48,317
Really?

326
00:17:49,359 --> 00:17:52,112
How's our mole in Camia's camp doing?

327
00:17:52,654 --> 00:17:54,573
Does she have any new information?

328
00:17:56,533 --> 00:17:57,910
See?

329
00:17:57,993 --> 00:17:59,620
You're taking too long, Emilia!

330
00:18:00,996 --> 00:18:02,498
I'm getting worried.

331
00:18:02,581 --> 00:18:05,417
I'm sure Camia's starting
to suspect that girl.

332
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:11,965
She wouldn't do such a thing
without a plan in mind.

333
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:15,344
Let's just trust her.

334
00:18:17,137 --> 00:18:18,180
Don't worry.

335
00:18:18,263 --> 00:18:19,723
I'll talk to her.

336
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:21,058
I'll ask her about her plan.

337
00:18:21,141 --> 00:18:22,768
I'll tell you everything.

338
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:26,480
Oh.

339
00:18:26,563 --> 00:18:28,774
I prepared some drinks and snacks.

340
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:30,359
Go ahead and eat.

341
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:33,278
[tense music playing]

342
00:18:45,457 --> 00:18:48,460
Um, I'll head back inside.

343
00:19:02,349 --> 00:19:04,059
-[Camia sighs]
-Aunt Camia, what's wrong?

344
00:19:04,893 --> 00:19:05,978
Diego.

345
00:19:07,771 --> 00:19:09,898
How well do you know Nimfa?

346
00:19:10,858 --> 00:19:12,734
Can we really trust her?

347
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:15,487
Nimfa and I grew up together.

348
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:21,493
I don't see any reason
why we shouldn't trust her.

349
00:19:25,038 --> 00:19:26,957
Why? Did something happen?

350
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:28,750
Did she do something?

351
00:19:29,459 --> 00:19:32,421
I'm sorry. I guess I'm just
being paranoid, Diego.

352
00:19:38,719 --> 00:19:40,971
[phone ringing]

353
00:19:41,054 --> 00:19:43,182
Speaking of the bitch, Aunt Claire.

354
00:19:48,562 --> 00:19:50,272
Hello, Nimfa?

355
00:19:50,355 --> 00:19:53,442
Well? I hope you have good news for us.

356
00:19:53,775 --> 00:19:56,862
[suspenseful music playing]

357
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:04,453
So?

358
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:06,371
What is it?

359
00:20:07,998 --> 00:20:10,667
Ivy and Arnaldo are now engaged.

360
00:20:10,751 --> 00:20:11,668
Oh, my.

361
00:20:11,752 --> 00:20:15,047
So, this is what the dinner
is all about, Aunt Claire.

362
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:17,716
[laughs]

363
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:19,176
Great.

364
00:20:19,718 --> 00:20:21,803
Ivy had better watch out.

365
00:20:22,804 --> 00:20:27,476
I have a plan, and she'll
regret saying yes to my son.

366
00:20:27,559 --> 00:20:30,479
[tense music playing]

367
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:36,151
[water running]

368
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:37,361
Nimfa.

369
00:20:38,153 --> 00:20:39,238
Diego.

370
00:20:39,863 --> 00:20:41,323
How are you doing here?

371
00:20:42,157 --> 00:20:43,325
I'm doing well.

372
00:20:43,742 --> 00:20:45,285
Miss Camia is kind.

373
00:20:45,786 --> 00:20:49,081
Even though I get a bit nosy.

374
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:51,708
Did she tell you about what I did?

375
00:20:53,043 --> 00:20:54,544
I'm really embarrassed.

376
00:20:55,045 --> 00:20:56,463
I'm so sorry, Diego.

377
00:20:57,464 --> 00:20:58,840
Don't worry. It's nothing.

378
00:21:00,592 --> 00:21:02,678
You know I trust you, right?

379
00:21:04,096 --> 00:21:07,391
So, I hope you won't do anything

380
00:21:07,474 --> 00:21:08,684
that'll ruin our friendship.

381
00:21:08,767 --> 00:21:11,186
[tense music playing]

382
00:21:12,604 --> 00:21:14,231
Okay. I have to go.

383
00:21:14,314 --> 00:21:15,399
Take care.

384
00:21:15,983 --> 00:21:17,067
Uh, Diego!

385
00:21:20,237 --> 00:21:22,656
You look troubled.

386
00:21:25,075 --> 00:21:26,285
I'm sorry again.

387
00:21:26,368 --> 00:21:28,620
I overheard your conversation
with Miss Camia.

388
00:21:30,247 --> 00:21:34,751
So, Miss Ivy and Mayor Arnaldo
are engaged.

389
00:21:38,630 --> 00:21:41,258
If you ever need someone
to talk to, I'm here.

390
00:21:45,387 --> 00:21:47,306
Oh, I have something to get from my house.

391
00:21:47,389 --> 00:21:48,724
Can you come with me?

392
00:21:49,141 --> 00:21:51,268
Let it out. It's not good to keep it in.

393
00:21:52,769 --> 00:21:54,104
Nimfa, I'm fine.

394
00:21:56,481 --> 00:21:59,359
You wouldn't let me
walk home alone, right?

395
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:01,528
Especially this late.

396
00:22:17,544 --> 00:22:18,712
Diego.

397
00:22:22,507 --> 00:22:24,885
Why do you let Ivy Aguas
affect you so much?

398
00:22:27,679 --> 00:22:29,723
Don't you ever think there's someone else

399
00:22:29,806 --> 00:22:31,349
who's better for you?

400
00:22:33,894 --> 00:22:37,397
A girl who can really love you.

401
00:22:37,731 --> 00:22:40,734
A girl who won't lead you on
like what Ivy's doing to you.

402
00:22:41,234 --> 00:22:43,945
[unsettling music playing]

403
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:46,490
A girl who can give you everything…

404
00:22:47,657 --> 00:22:49,576
and who'll do everything for you.

405
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:53,121
Diego.

406
00:22:54,164 --> 00:22:57,959
Just say the word, and I'll be that girl.

407
00:22:58,460 --> 00:23:01,755
[unsettling music playing]

408
00:23:12,015 --> 00:23:13,100
Nimfa, wait.

409
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:16,478
We're just friends.

410
00:23:17,854 --> 00:23:20,190
Can we not ruin what we have?

411
00:23:22,734 --> 00:23:24,111
[car door opens]

412
00:23:28,031 --> 00:23:29,241
Nimfa, go home.

413
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:32,369
[tense music playing]

414
00:24:00,188 --> 00:24:01,606
[Claire] This is really good, right?

415
00:24:01,690 --> 00:24:02,691
[Julio] Yeah.

416
00:24:03,150 --> 00:24:06,444
Well, it's supposed to be
a special dinner because…

417
00:24:07,154 --> 00:24:08,446
Arnaldo.

418
00:24:09,156 --> 00:24:10,699
We've had a good meal.

419
00:24:11,158 --> 00:24:17,122
Now, you said you were going to have
an announcement to make?

420
00:24:17,205 --> 00:24:19,166
Yes, Grandpa. I have
an announcement to make.

421
00:24:19,249 --> 00:24:22,919
Rather, we have an announcement to make.

422
00:24:23,003 --> 00:24:25,881
[suspenseful music playing]

423
00:24:28,049 --> 00:24:29,342
Go on.

424
00:24:29,426 --> 00:24:33,263
But before you make that announcement,
I have a surprise for both of you.

425
00:24:33,346 --> 00:24:34,181
Hold on.

426
00:24:34,264 --> 00:24:36,892
[Emilia] Jenny! Jenny!

427
00:24:38,685 --> 00:24:39,811
Please, bring it out.

428
00:24:39,895 --> 00:24:41,646
I didn't see this coming.

429
00:24:44,816 --> 00:24:45,817
A cake?

430
00:24:48,445 --> 00:24:50,155
Surprise!

431
00:24:52,324 --> 00:24:55,118
Congratulations on your engagement, Ivy.

432
00:24:55,202 --> 00:24:58,163
[tense music playing]

433
00:25:07,380 --> 00:25:08,798
How thoughtful of you, Emilia.

434
00:25:08,882 --> 00:25:11,259
But where's the bride's head?

435
00:25:12,385 --> 00:25:13,511
[chuckles]

436
00:25:13,595 --> 00:25:15,597
Isn't it obvious, Ivy?

437
00:25:16,848 --> 00:25:19,267
It's obvious you don't
like me for Arnaldo,

438
00:25:19,351 --> 00:25:20,810
that's why you'll do everything

439
00:25:20,894 --> 00:25:23,230
to get in the way of our relationship.

440
00:25:23,563 --> 00:25:25,690
Yes. Oh, wait.

441
00:25:26,233 --> 00:25:28,526
That's exactly what I wanted to say.

442
00:25:29,277 --> 00:25:30,403
[Julio] Emilia.

443
00:25:31,029 --> 00:25:33,281
-It's okay, Congressman.
-I'm so sorry.

444
00:25:33,365 --> 00:25:34,658
No. It's okay, hon.

445
00:25:34,741 --> 00:25:36,868
But I guess I need to go home, Arnaldo.

446
00:25:36,952 --> 00:25:38,870
I'm not welcome in this house.

447
00:25:38,954 --> 00:25:41,748
-And we're done.
-Excuse me. Excuse me.

448
00:25:43,041 --> 00:25:45,043
Oh, wait. Let me escort you out.

449
00:25:45,377 --> 00:25:48,797
Because aside from my son,

450
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:50,757
you might end up seducing our guards too.

451
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:53,093
Emilia, please.

452
00:25:54,678 --> 00:25:55,971
It's okay.

453
00:25:58,890 --> 00:25:59,975
Excuse me.

454
00:26:03,103 --> 00:26:05,021
Emilia, I said excuse me.

455
00:26:08,108 --> 00:26:11,152
[tense music playing]

456
00:26:17,575 --> 00:26:19,661
-[grunts]
-[shrieks]

457
00:26:19,744 --> 00:26:20,745
-Stop it!
-Emilia.

458
00:26:20,829 --> 00:26:23,873
You can cross anyone but not me!

459
00:26:26,001 --> 00:26:27,377
-Stop it.
-Stop them!

460
00:26:27,460 --> 00:26:28,712
You're really getting on my nerves!

461
00:26:28,795 --> 00:26:30,338
-Ivy, that's enough!
-Stop it, Ivy!

462
00:26:30,422 --> 00:26:32,382
-Stop it! Stop it!
-Ivy! That's enough!

463
00:26:32,465 --> 00:26:33,758
-Don't try to stop me!
-Mom!

464
00:26:33,842 --> 00:26:35,468
Arnaldo, take Ivy away from here.

465
00:26:35,552 --> 00:26:38,555
I said stop it!

466
00:26:39,347 --> 00:26:40,807
-Arnaldo!
-Please, that's enough!

467
00:26:40,890 --> 00:26:41,975
The two of you! Stop it!

468
00:26:42,058 --> 00:26:43,476
You want to chop my head off?

469
00:26:43,560 --> 00:26:45,478
Not if I chop yours first!

470
00:26:45,562 --> 00:26:48,356
Enough, enough, enough! Ivy.
Come here. Please.

471
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:49,983
Please!

472
00:26:50,066 --> 00:26:51,693
Don't try me, Emilia.

473
00:26:51,776 --> 00:26:52,777
Not me!

474
00:26:52,861 --> 00:26:55,155
-The both of you, stop it!
-We aren't done yet!

475
00:26:55,238 --> 00:26:56,197
Remember this!

476
00:26:56,281 --> 00:26:57,490
I'm gonna do everything

477
00:26:57,574 --> 00:26:59,200
to ruin your engagement with my son!

478
00:26:59,284 --> 00:27:00,910
Bring it on!

479
00:27:00,994 --> 00:27:02,495
-Arnaldo, take Ivy outside!
-Let me go!

480
00:27:02,579 --> 00:27:03,913
Get out of my house!

481
00:27:03,997 --> 00:27:05,582
I won't leave

482
00:27:05,665 --> 00:27:08,668
because I will be the
new queen of this mansion.

483
00:27:08,752 --> 00:27:09,502
[Emilia laughing]

484
00:27:09,586 --> 00:27:13,465
[Julio] Is this really
the future of this family?

485
00:27:14,257 --> 00:27:15,425
Look at you!

486
00:27:15,508 --> 00:27:20,055
Supposed educated women of the society.

487
00:27:20,597 --> 00:27:22,182
Look how you're acting!

488
00:27:22,265 --> 00:27:24,517
You're worse than animals in a jungle!

489
00:27:25,769 --> 00:27:29,481
I have seen women of ill repute

490
00:27:29,564 --> 00:27:31,649
behave better than the two of you!

491
00:27:32,359 --> 00:27:34,361
You're worse than prostitutes

492
00:27:34,444 --> 00:27:36,071
getting at each other's throats!

493
00:27:36,654 --> 00:27:41,326
A classic example of a lowlife catfight!

494
00:27:42,243 --> 00:27:44,704
Is this the future of my life?

495
00:27:44,788 --> 00:27:47,582
For me to have a daughter who is a bitch,

496
00:27:47,665 --> 00:27:50,919
and another bitch for a daughter-in-law?!

497
00:27:52,253 --> 00:27:54,547
Dirty doesn't even come close

498
00:27:54,631 --> 00:27:56,966
to what you've shown here tonight!

499
00:27:58,802 --> 00:28:00,011
Shame on you!

500
00:28:01,346 --> 00:28:03,973
Shame on both of you!

501
00:28:06,267 --> 00:28:07,602
Animals!

502
00:28:08,353 --> 00:28:10,730
I never thought I'd see the day.

503
00:28:11,147 --> 00:28:14,609
[tense music playing]

504
00:28:21,241 --> 00:28:22,450
[Emilia groans]

505
00:28:23,618 --> 00:28:27,288
[tense music playing]

506
00:28:31,459 --> 00:28:33,211
Thank you, hon. Thank you.

507
00:28:33,753 --> 00:28:35,255
I'm sorry.

508
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:37,257
You know, your mom…

509
00:28:37,340 --> 00:28:39,676
-I know. I'm sorry.
-I'm sorry, hon.

510
00:28:39,759 --> 00:28:43,138
I didn't mean to do it. [sobbing]

511
00:28:43,221 --> 00:28:45,724
You saw what she did, right?

512
00:28:45,807 --> 00:28:47,600
-Yes.
-She started it.

513
00:28:47,684 --> 00:28:49,811
I know. It's not your fault. I'm sorry.

514
00:28:50,228 --> 00:28:53,064
I'm sorry, Arnaldo.
I didn't want this to happen.

515
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:56,192
Congressman, I'm sorry.

516
00:28:56,276 --> 00:28:59,112
[tense music playing]

517
00:28:59,696 --> 00:29:01,239
Stop crying, hon.

518
00:29:01,865 --> 00:29:03,992
[sobbing]

519
00:29:08,246 --> 00:29:10,248
[fakes sobbing]

520
00:29:13,460 --> 00:29:16,171
Oh, that woman! I swear!

521
00:29:17,839 --> 00:29:19,966
You know what, Emilia? You shouldn't have

522
00:29:20,049 --> 00:29:21,634
insulted her in the first place.

523
00:29:21,718 --> 00:29:24,387
Look what happened to you.
So, how's the cake?

524
00:29:24,471 --> 00:29:26,973
Oh, quit it. I'll kill that woman!

525
00:29:28,016 --> 00:29:29,225
Calm down, Emilia!

526
00:29:29,559 --> 00:29:31,644
Think about the repercussions
of what you did!

527
00:29:32,228 --> 00:29:33,980
Julio will be mad at you.

528
00:29:34,439 --> 00:29:36,149
[Claire] Arnaldo is the golden boy.

529
00:29:37,942 --> 00:29:39,444
And you, Emilia…

530
00:29:40,236 --> 00:29:42,989
of all the Ardientes I know,

531
00:29:43,072 --> 00:29:44,949
you're the one who never learned anything

532
00:29:45,033 --> 00:29:46,910
from what I've taught you!

533
00:29:48,161 --> 00:29:50,705
-Papa…
-You know why?

534
00:29:51,164 --> 00:29:54,417
You always act before you think!

535
00:29:54,501 --> 00:29:55,668
What's wrong with you?

536
00:29:55,752 --> 00:29:58,087
I just don't trust that woman!

537
00:29:58,171 --> 00:29:59,714
Neither do I!

538
00:30:00,173 --> 00:30:01,591
I don't trust her.

539
00:30:01,674 --> 00:30:03,176
But, did I ever show her that?

540
00:30:03,259 --> 00:30:04,928
Of course not. Why?

541
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:07,847
Because we need her.

542
00:30:08,598 --> 00:30:12,018
How many times do I have
to tell you all that?

543
00:30:12,602 --> 00:30:14,270
Or do I have to hit you with this

544
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:15,730
so you finally learn your lesson?

545
00:30:15,814 --> 00:30:17,106
Emilia!

546
00:30:18,441 --> 00:30:19,359
[groans]

547
00:30:19,442 --> 00:30:22,028
[tense music playing]

548
00:30:24,072 --> 00:30:25,949
[Julio] Your head's up your butt!

549
00:30:27,867 --> 00:30:30,787
I'll make sure to uncover
that woman's dirt!

550
00:30:32,455 --> 00:30:34,165
Especially now.

551
00:30:35,458 --> 00:30:37,085
She better watch her back.

552
00:30:37,168 --> 00:30:39,921
[tense music playing]

553
00:30:40,004 --> 00:30:41,005
[grunts]

554
00:30:46,886 --> 00:30:48,012
[sighs]

555
00:30:49,222 --> 00:30:50,598
[deep sigh]

556
00:30:50,682 --> 00:30:52,934
-Here.
-I'm still shaking.

557
00:30:53,476 --> 00:30:55,478
Hon, I'll be fine. Thank you.

558
00:30:56,354 --> 00:30:57,605
Thank you.

559
00:30:58,731 --> 00:31:00,024
Thank you, hon.

560
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:01,943
Um…

561
00:31:04,279 --> 00:31:06,447
I think it'd be better if I just go home.

562
00:31:07,532 --> 00:31:10,201
I don't really feel that
I'm welcome in this house.

563
00:31:11,870 --> 00:31:13,746
Please? I need to go home.

564
00:31:13,830 --> 00:31:16,666
No. You're not going home, okay?

565
00:31:17,083 --> 00:31:18,585
Stay here for the night.

566
00:31:18,668 --> 00:31:19,878
Hon.

567
00:31:21,337 --> 00:31:22,338
[sighs]

568
00:31:23,298 --> 00:31:25,466
This is just so painful.

569
00:31:29,053 --> 00:31:31,472
My heart's still racing, hon.

570
00:31:33,057 --> 00:31:36,060
How did this even happen?

571
00:31:37,020 --> 00:31:39,230
It's just embarrassing. I don't want this.

572
00:31:39,314 --> 00:31:45,069
I don't want to fight with
my future mother-in-law.

573
00:31:46,654 --> 00:31:50,158
I guess, Emilia and I
will never get along, so…

574
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:56,122
Let's just call off the wedding.

575
00:31:57,624 --> 00:32:00,376
Maybe we aren't meant
for each other, Arnaldo.

576
00:32:00,460 --> 00:32:03,463
No, no. Hey! That's nonsense, okay?

577
00:32:03,546 --> 00:32:04,297
Hon.

578
00:32:04,380 --> 00:32:06,299
No. Don't ever think about that.

579
00:32:06,382 --> 00:32:09,135
No one else deserves my love, but you.

580
00:32:09,594 --> 00:32:12,388
No other woman deserves me, but you.

581
00:32:12,472 --> 00:32:14,140
Don't ever think that way.

582
00:32:14,807 --> 00:32:16,017
Oh, hon.

583
00:32:18,728 --> 00:32:19,979
You know what?

584
00:32:21,648 --> 00:32:24,609
I… I really think Mom's just insecure

585
00:32:25,652 --> 00:32:27,862
because she will never be as
powerful and as wealthy

586
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:28,947
as you are.

587
00:32:29,030 --> 00:32:30,573
That's why she's always targeting you.

588
00:32:30,657 --> 00:32:31,574
Of course not.

589
00:32:31,658 --> 00:32:35,370
Your mom is an ex-governor,
and she's an Ardiente.

590
00:32:35,453 --> 00:32:36,913
That means she's wealthy.

591
00:32:36,996 --> 00:32:40,583
Well, our family is rich, but she isn't.

592
00:32:42,460 --> 00:32:43,795
What?

593
00:32:44,462 --> 00:32:45,838
You mean…

594
00:32:46,881 --> 00:32:49,676
Emilia doesn't have her own money?

595
00:32:49,759 --> 00:32:50,885
[scoffs]

596
00:32:52,387 --> 00:32:53,471
She doesn't.

597
00:32:54,347 --> 00:32:56,516
Besides, she doesn't know where

598
00:32:56,599 --> 00:32:58,059
Grandpa's keeping our money.

599
00:32:59,435 --> 00:33:01,062
Overseas accounts?

600
00:33:02,105 --> 00:33:04,649
Overseas accounts, as you already know,

601
00:33:04,732 --> 00:33:07,652
are hard to maintain,
so we prefer it nearby

602
00:33:07,735 --> 00:33:09,529
and easily accessible.

603
00:33:11,781 --> 00:33:15,576
Hon, aren't you afraid
the banks will be able

604
00:33:15,660 --> 00:33:17,203
to trace all your wealth?

605
00:33:17,286 --> 00:33:18,788
That's risky.

606
00:33:18,871 --> 00:33:20,498
Who said our money's in the bank?

607
00:33:22,458 --> 00:33:26,170
We prefer stacking it in piles
and counting it by millions.

608
00:33:29,257 --> 00:33:30,466
Good idea.

609
00:33:32,677 --> 00:33:34,721
-I'm still shaking.
-Have some water.

610
00:33:34,804 --> 00:33:37,598
-I'm really sorry, hon.
-No. Stop saying sorry.

611
00:33:37,682 --> 00:33:38,850
It's not your fault.

612
00:33:39,267 --> 00:33:41,060
I didn't mean to hurt your mother.

613
00:33:41,144 --> 00:33:42,937
You know how much I love you, right?

614
00:33:43,021 --> 00:33:44,564
-I know.
-I love you, hon.

615
00:33:44,647 --> 00:33:46,274
-I know.
-I love you.

616
00:33:46,357 --> 00:33:48,109
[unsettling music playing]

617
00:33:51,946 --> 00:33:53,990
[ominous music playing]

618
00:34:05,376 --> 00:34:06,961
Ivy will stay here tonight.

619
00:34:08,171 --> 00:34:09,714
I asked her to stay

620
00:34:09,797 --> 00:34:12,550
because something might happen
to her on her way home.

621
00:34:14,594 --> 00:34:16,471
Oh, and by the way,
this will be the last time

622
00:34:16,554 --> 00:34:17,430
you'll disrespect her.

623
00:34:19,599 --> 00:34:20,641
Apologize to her.

624
00:34:22,143 --> 00:34:24,562
Over my dead body, Arnaldo!

625
00:34:25,438 --> 00:34:27,148
I will not apologize to her!

626
00:34:27,231 --> 00:34:29,609
She started everything
when she smashed a cake--

627
00:34:29,692 --> 00:34:30,777
Enough!

628
00:34:32,153 --> 00:34:34,655
I'm sick and tired of
hearing all your nonsense.

629
00:34:36,491 --> 00:34:37,784
That woman will soon be my wife

630
00:34:37,867 --> 00:34:39,077
and the future mother of my children.

631
00:34:39,160 --> 00:34:40,536
Apologize to her…

632
00:34:41,412 --> 00:34:42,789
or else you're going to lose a son…

633
00:34:45,458 --> 00:34:47,502
and gain one more enemy on your list.

634
00:34:48,586 --> 00:34:51,839
This is unbelievable, Arnaldo!
You are unbelievable!

635
00:34:51,923 --> 00:34:55,009
[tense music playing]

636
00:35:06,229 --> 00:35:08,773
[Arnaldo] <i>Overseas accounts,</i>
<i>as you already know,</i>

637
00:35:08,856 --> 00:35:09,774
<i>are hard to maintain.</i>

638
00:35:09,857 --> 00:35:13,444
<i>So, we prefer it nearby</i>
<i>and easily accessible.</i>

639
00:35:13,528 --> 00:35:15,363
<i>Aren't you afraid the banks will be able</i>

640
00:35:15,446 --> 00:35:17,073
<i>to trace all your wealth?</i>

641
00:35:17,156 --> 00:35:19,367
<i>Who said our money's in the bank?</i>

642
00:35:19,450 --> 00:35:23,329
<i>We prefer stacking it in piles</i>
<i>and counting it by millions.</i>

643
00:35:24,997 --> 00:35:29,460
<i>The Ardientes are being</i>
<i>protected by their wealth.</i>

644
00:35:30,044 --> 00:35:32,004
<i>Taking that from them</i>

645
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:36,134
<i>will weaken their very core.</i>

646
00:35:36,217 --> 00:35:38,970
[tense music playing]

647
00:35:42,181 --> 00:35:44,684
<i>Where could they have hidden</i>

648
00:35:44,767 --> 00:35:47,395
<i>their money within this mansion?</i>

649
00:35:50,940 --> 00:35:52,024
[Diego] Thanks.

650
00:35:57,655 --> 00:36:00,658
[pensive music playing]

651
00:36:14,964 --> 00:36:18,176
[soft music playing]

652
00:36:28,436 --> 00:36:31,981
[phone rings]

653
00:36:38,779 --> 00:36:39,989
Diego?

654
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:42,575
Ivy, how are you doing?

655
00:36:43,868 --> 00:36:44,994
Uh…

656
00:36:46,954 --> 00:36:48,414
I'm fine.

657
00:36:49,332 --> 00:36:52,418
<i>I'm at the Ardientes' mansion.</i>

658
00:36:53,419 --> 00:36:55,213
Uh, Diego…

659
00:36:56,255 --> 00:36:57,089
<i>Um…</i>

660
00:36:58,549 --> 00:37:01,135
Arnaldo just told me about this.

661
00:37:01,802 --> 00:37:03,262
<i>Now I'm wondering.</i>

662
00:37:04,263 --> 00:37:06,974
The Ardientes don't have their money

663
00:37:07,058 --> 00:37:10,019
kept in a bank here or overseas.

664
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:13,022
Did you know that?

665
00:37:13,439 --> 00:37:15,524
Why are you suddenly so interested?

666
00:37:16,442 --> 00:37:17,985
<i>What are you planning, Ivy?</i>

667
00:37:19,445 --> 00:37:21,364
You're in the home of murderers.

668
00:37:21,447 --> 00:37:22,782
<i>You have to be careful.</i>

669
00:37:22,865 --> 00:37:24,742
Like I said…

670
00:37:25,660 --> 00:37:27,370
I can take care of myself.

671
00:37:27,453 --> 00:37:29,705
I know where the guards are stationed…

672
00:37:29,789 --> 00:37:31,540
<i>and where the CCTV cameras are located.</i>

673
00:37:32,250 --> 00:37:34,085
I know how to get past them.

674
00:37:34,168 --> 00:37:37,296
Thanks for checking up on me.
But it's getting late.

675
00:37:37,546 --> 00:37:38,798
Ivy?

676
00:37:38,881 --> 00:37:41,592
[tense music playing]

677
00:37:43,886 --> 00:37:46,889
[suspenseful music playing]

678
00:38:06,742 --> 00:38:09,662
[suspenseful music playing]

679
00:38:23,676 --> 00:38:26,887
[suspenseful music playing]

680
00:38:45,531 --> 00:38:48,659
[suspenseful music playing]

681
00:39:04,884 --> 00:39:06,010
Ivy?

682
00:39:09,055 --> 00:39:10,264
Ivy!

683
00:39:19,607 --> 00:39:22,526
[suspenseful music playing]

684
00:39:32,745 --> 00:39:33,871
Ivy?

685
00:39:35,664 --> 00:39:36,832
Ivy?

686
00:39:36,916 --> 00:39:40,002
[suspenseful music playing]

687
00:40:13,744 --> 00:40:16,997
[tense music playing]

688
00:40:29,135 --> 00:40:31,011
Ivy, it's me, Diego.

689
00:40:32,888 --> 00:40:34,640
-Diego.
-Come here.

690
00:40:34,723 --> 00:40:37,685
[tense music playing]

691
00:40:45,734 --> 00:40:47,445
I knew it!

692
00:40:48,988 --> 00:40:50,698
Hey, Ivy.

693
00:40:51,282 --> 00:40:54,493
I'll find you, and I will catch you.

694
00:40:58,456 --> 00:41:00,499
[line rings]

695
00:41:01,459 --> 00:41:03,002
Hello? Ramirez.

696
00:41:03,669 --> 00:41:04,712
Report to me immediately.

697
00:41:04,795 --> 00:41:07,756
We need to catch someone. Hurry up.

698
00:41:08,174 --> 00:41:10,634
[ominous music playing]

699
00:41:10,718 --> 00:41:12,720
[Emilia] You thought
you could hide from me?

700
00:41:13,554 --> 00:41:16,307
I will find you, Ivy.

701
00:41:16,682 --> 00:41:18,100
[hums teasingly]

702
00:41:18,184 --> 00:41:21,145
[ominous music playing]

703
00:41:29,737 --> 00:41:32,323
<i>Please protect</i>
<i>my daughter from our enemies.</i>

704
00:41:37,161 --> 00:41:37,912
Yes, ma'am?

705
00:41:37,995 --> 00:41:40,289
Ramirez, what took you so long? Hurry!

706
00:41:40,372 --> 00:41:42,583
Search every inch of that building.

707
00:41:42,666 --> 00:41:43,918
Find Ivy Aguas.

708
00:41:44,001 --> 00:41:45,461
-All right.
-Hurry up!

709
00:41:46,545 --> 00:41:49,048
Hmm… I'm coming to get you.

710
00:41:49,131 --> 00:41:51,800
[tense music playing]

711
00:41:54,762 --> 00:41:56,180
[man] That way.

712
00:41:58,474 --> 00:41:59,850
Jenny?

713
00:42:00,684 --> 00:42:01,685
Ma'am?

714
00:42:01,769 --> 00:42:03,145
Is that you, Jenny?

715
00:42:04,772 --> 00:42:06,023
Jenny!

716
00:42:06,941 --> 00:42:08,817
Seriously, Jenny?!

717
00:42:09,818 --> 00:42:10,778
[Jenny] Ma'am, I'm sorry.

718
00:42:10,861 --> 00:42:14,490
If you two want to hook up,
do it in your rooms!

719
00:42:14,573 --> 00:42:16,033
You're disgusting, Fabian!

720
00:42:17,660 --> 00:42:18,827
[Emilia] Unbelievable!

721
00:42:19,453 --> 00:42:22,164
Ramirez, look for Ivy in the back.

722
00:42:22,248 --> 00:42:23,666
-Yes, ma'am.
-Keep your eyes peeled!

723
00:42:23,749 --> 00:42:24,542
Yes, ma'am.

724
00:42:24,625 --> 00:42:27,545
[tense music playing]

725
00:42:39,348 --> 00:42:42,268
[suspenseful music playing]

726
00:42:51,860 --> 00:42:52,987
Emilia.

727
00:42:57,116 --> 00:42:58,701
What are you doing there?

728
00:42:59,368 --> 00:43:00,995
I'm looking for something.

729
00:43:01,078 --> 00:43:03,747
[Raul] At this hour? Let's go back inside.

730
00:43:05,165 --> 00:43:06,667
Come on.

731
00:43:06,750 --> 00:43:07,918
It's late.

732
00:43:08,002 --> 00:43:11,005
[mellow music playing]

733
00:43:45,164 --> 00:43:47,333
Go on, Ivy. Go back to your room.

734
00:43:47,958 --> 00:43:49,084
Diego, be careful.

735
00:43:49,168 --> 00:43:50,669
I will. Go inside!

736
00:43:51,378 --> 00:43:52,588
Thank you.

737
00:43:52,671 --> 00:43:55,674
[mellow music playing]

738
00:43:58,927 --> 00:44:00,179
[whispers] Go on.

739
00:44:19,657 --> 00:44:24,119
Well, well, well… And another well.

740
00:44:25,037 --> 00:44:26,455
Where have you been?

741
00:44:27,539 --> 00:44:29,667
Why are you out of breath?

742
00:44:31,001 --> 00:44:34,088
Wait. Who did you seduce this time?

743
00:44:34,505 --> 00:44:36,674
A, the guards?

744
00:44:37,049 --> 00:44:39,051
B, Madrigal?

745
00:44:39,551 --> 00:44:41,512
Or letter C, Diego?

746
00:44:42,054 --> 00:44:45,766
[dramatic music playing]

747
00:44:48,477 --> 00:44:49,853
You know, Ivy…

748
00:44:50,646 --> 00:44:52,689
you can't fool me.

749
00:44:55,025 --> 00:44:57,194
Well, I'm not trying to fool you.

750
00:44:58,612 --> 00:45:02,116
I just came from Arnaldo's room.

751
00:45:02,825 --> 00:45:04,618
I couldn't help myself.

752
00:45:07,162 --> 00:45:08,288
What?

753
00:45:10,165 --> 00:45:12,501
If you don't want to believe me…

754
00:45:12,584 --> 00:45:13,961
Um…

755
00:45:14,044 --> 00:45:15,087
Oops.

756
00:45:15,170 --> 00:45:16,463
[snickers]

757
00:45:17,673 --> 00:45:21,301
Or do you want me to wake Arnaldo up so…

758
00:45:21,385 --> 00:45:25,472
But, Emilia, your son's worn out.

759
00:45:30,436 --> 00:45:31,770
Emilia…

760
00:45:32,354 --> 00:45:35,983
My future mother-in-law,
let's stop fighting.

761
00:45:36,942 --> 00:45:40,404
And I'm sorry for what
happened at dinner earlier.

762
00:45:40,946 --> 00:45:43,031
I'm sorry, my future mother-in-law.

763
00:45:43,574 --> 00:45:45,451
I don't want us to fight.

764
00:45:46,160 --> 00:45:47,286
But…

765
00:45:49,538 --> 00:45:52,666
[sighs] If you don't stop
breathing down my neck,

766
00:45:53,667 --> 00:45:55,085
you know that…

767
00:45:56,753 --> 00:45:58,338
I won't back down.

768
00:46:00,507 --> 00:46:05,012
I'll take what little you still have left.

769
00:46:06,013 --> 00:46:07,848
It won't just stress you out,

770
00:46:07,931 --> 00:46:10,100
you might go into depression too.

771
00:46:10,184 --> 00:46:12,811
[tense music playing]

772
00:46:20,235 --> 00:46:21,820
[Diego] <i>Arnaldo is the key</i>

773
00:46:21,904 --> 00:46:24,490
<i>to finding where</i>
<i>they're keeping their money.</i>

774
00:46:27,743 --> 00:46:29,077
<i>Proceed with the plan.</i>

775
00:46:29,161 --> 00:46:30,829
<i>Julio Ardiente's head is mine.</i>

776
00:46:30,913 --> 00:46:32,581
<i>I will kill him myself.</i>

777
00:46:32,664 --> 00:46:35,584
[Emilia] <i>I have no patience</i>
<i>for Ivy, Aunt Claire.</i>

778
00:46:35,667 --> 00:46:37,920
<i>I have to resort back to my old tricks.</i>

779
00:46:38,003 --> 00:46:40,255
[Claire] <i>Like what you did to Camia Cruz?</i>

780
00:46:40,339 --> 00:46:42,174
<i>Are you ready for your new assignment?</i>

781
00:46:42,257 --> 00:46:43,217
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

782
00:46:43,300 --> 00:46:45,010
<i>Ivy agreed to have dinner with you.</i>

783
00:46:45,093 --> 00:46:46,845
<i>Are you excited for our dinner?</i>

784
00:46:46,929 --> 00:46:49,014
<i>-Of course.</i>
<i>-I shall see you.</i>

785
00:46:49,848 --> 00:46:52,476
<i>I'm very excited, Emilia.</i>

786
00:46:52,559 --> 00:46:56,188
[theme music playing]
